 Synthesis of AgNPs
The aqueous extract of E. camaldulensis was prepared by mixing 10 g of dry leaf sample with 100 mL of highly purified water. The mixture was heated for 10 min at 80 °C to denature the enzymes in the extract. The solution was filtered through a Whatman filter paper No. 1 (pore size 125 mm). The supernatant (filtrate) was further filtered through a Whatman filter paper No. 1 (pore size 25 mm) to remove the remaining plant residues. For synthesis of the AgNPs, 12 mL aqueous leaf extract of E. camaldulensis were mixed with 88 mL of 1 mmol/L AgNO3 solution in an Erlenmeyer flask and allowed to react at room temperature for 24 h. The AgNPs extract was stored at 4 °C until further analysis.
